          "path": "/content/entityContext/2",
          "kind": "hypothesis",
          "rationale": "Disabling assignment until task cues are visible is a proposed interface safeguard, not a supplied requirement or observed behavior."
        }
      ],
      "content": {
        "summary": "CURRENT in the constructed inventory: the list exposes work-order ID, zone, severity, age, and crew; one detail can be opened and one crew assigned there. REQUIRED by the synthetic task: preserve the selected ID and expose severity and age before assignment, with WCAG 2.2 AA. PROPOSED UI: show a selected-order context header in detail and a return path to the list. UNRESOLVED: whether detail refreshes severity, age, or assignment and how errors or authorization work; no deployed behavior is established.",
        "navigation": [
          "Current: work-order list → selected work-order detail; assignment action is present in detail.",
          "Proposed: detail → work-order list return action retaining a visible selected ID cue; test the actual return behavior before treating it as current."
        ],
        "terminology": [
          "Work order means one identified water-leak service item; use its exact ID in list and detail.",
          "Severity, age, and assigned crew use the inventory's terms and values; no new status taxonomy is defined."
        ],
        "entityContext": [
          "Required: show the same exact work-order ID on the selected list item, detail header, and pre-assignment action context.",
          "Required: show severity and age for that ID before crew assignment; identify when values came from the list rather than claiming an unobserved detail refresh.",
          "Proposed UI safeguard: keep the assignment action unavailable until the ID, severity, and age cues are visible; validate whether this gate helps dispatchers.",
          "Proposed: keep zone and current crew visible as supporting context; unresolved freshness, authorization, and assignment result must be surfaced rather than assumed."
        ],
        "accessibilityBaseline": "WCAG 2.2 AA"
      }
    },
    {
